From f179a2c524e69fec5e2b7ee4b05ca950c84cb48e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marcell Matthias Haritopoulos <marcell.haritopoulos@student.tugraz.at>
Date: Sat, 3 Jan 2026 00:01:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 10/13] filemap: readahead: add page cache isolation for faults
 (broken async)

Implement sync and async I/O mimicking. While sync works (albeit pretty
slow with the currentyl created/destroyed temp fake mappings, but async
is very prone to crashing.
async does for some reason work with a shared fake address_space
instance. While it does not cleanly isolate the state that way, include
it for now to move on with the impl, and break it up later (or keep
async readahead disabled).

filemap: skip non-accessed folios in folios on vm op map_pages
---
 fs/inode.c              |  17 ++
 include/linux/fs.h      |   3 +
 include/linux/pagemap.h |  10 +
 mm/filemap.c            | 577 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 mm/readahead.c          | 128 ++++++---
 5 files changed, 647 insertions(+), 88 deletions(-)

